<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/12th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">The Anarchy</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1138–1153</span> · <a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Anarchy was a civil war in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a> and Normandy between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/stephen-king-of-england">King Stephen</a> and Empress Matilda, daughter of Henry I, over the succession to the English throne. Fighting, sieges and the breakdown of royal authority lasted from 1138 until the Treaty of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wallingford">Wallingford</a> of 1153, which made Matilda's son Henry heir to Stephen. Henry II's accession in 1154 restored strong royal government.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/the-anarchy.jpg" alt="The Anarchy" width="320" height="229" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:BattleOf_Lincoln.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
